# Spacetime as dissipative emergence: anchor-free mechanics and the tick-selection locus

## Claim

Three statements, formalized jointly as the framework's emergence
picture. Each is a composition of results already canonical; the
contribution of this doc is the names and the assembly, not new
derivation content.

**(S1) Spacetime is the dissipative emergence of Planck-scale
dynamics.** The continuum 3+1 manifold — metric, signature, spatial
dimension, and arrow — is the coarse-grained shadow of a first-order,
irreversible, per-Planck-tick substrate update. The emergence
mechanism is dissipation itself: eliminating the tick's binary Z₂
index *manufactures* the second-order wave operator `∂²_t`
(`tick_continuum_construction.md`, exact Goldstein–Kac identity), and
the residual first-order friction `2λ ∂_tφ` is the arrow of time
surfacing in the continuum — predicted, not anomalous.

**(S2) The mechanics are anchor-free.** Every structure-producing
step — mediant insertion, action-weighted tick sampling, dissipative
gradient flow, Z₆ mode counting, the rational-field-equation fixed
point — takes zero observational inputs. The two anchors (H₀, v_EW;
Lemma 3 of `structural_lemmas.md`) are read-out addresses: they
locate the observer on the structure when predictions are expressed
in dimensionful units, and they never enter the mechanics. This is
the README's address-vs-structure distinction formalized at the level
of the dynamics, and it preserves — does not contradict — the
two-anchor minimum.

**(S3) Probability enters the mechanics at exactly one locus — the
tick selection — and the Born rule is that locus's derived measure,
not a postulate.** The **tick selection** is the per-Planck-tick
choice among admissible mediant transitions, weighted by
`exp(−S_token)` (`f_exit_natural.md`); at the binary level it is the
saddle-node branch choice, the Z₂ winding-sign `s = ±1`
(`born_rule_parameter_free.md` #TICK(a),
`tick_continuum_construction.md`). Every other element of the
dynamics is deterministic dissipative flow under the action-weighted
lens: the path of least action is written into the dynamics rather
than imposed as a variational axiom.

