| Mediant insertion (Stern-Brocot) | two locked fractions | none — forced by conservation + stability |
| Tick selection weighting | `exp(−S_token)`, S in Planck units (ℏ = 1) | none — dimensionless action |
| Dissipative gradient flow | cost landscape `C(ψ)` | none — landscape is structural |
| Z₆ mode counting / filters | `q₂ = 2, q₃ = 3` | none — `qd_origins.md` |
| Rational-field-equation fixed point | mode populations, tongue widths | none — dimensionless self-consistency |

No step consumes H₀, v_EW, or any measured quantity. The mechanics
close on themselves: the fixed point is "the distribution determines
the coupling which determines the distribution"
(`PROOF_A_gravity.md` P4), a dimensionless self-consistency
condition with no external scale.

This does **not** reduce the anchor count below two. Lemma 3 stands:
expressing *where on the structure we are* — any dimensionful
prediction — requires H₀ (K = 1 sector) and v_EW (K < 1 sector),
and "an anchor cannot be substrate-derived by definition — deriving
it ⇒ it is not an anchor" (`anchor_count_reaudit.md`). S2 and
Lemma 3 are the same feature seen from its two sides:

- **Mechanics side (S2):** the structure-producing dynamics take
  zero anchor inputs — anchors do not appear in any forcing
  argument.
- **Read-out side (Lemma 3):** translating structure into
  dimensionful observables takes exactly two anchor inputs, one per
