## What this does not establish

1. **The magnitude of λ** (how nearly reversible the continuum
   shadow is) — the one quantitative residual of the tick
   construction (`tick_continuum_construction.md`).
2. **The (A)/(B) fork.** Whether tick selection is stochastic or
   deterministic remains open; the settling computation (explicit
   token-sequence derivation from the BOS state) has not been done
   (`substrate_determinism.md`).
3. **Why action-weighted sampling.** The Boltzmann lens is a
   committed form, not derived (`f_exit_natural.md`).
4. **Empirical probability distributions.** The framework still
   owes computed distributions matched to measured histograms; this
   gap is independent of the fork (`substrate_determinism.md`).
5. **Mean-field closure.** The nonlinear coefficient of the tick
   construction uses the standard hydrodynamic closure
   (`⟨sin φ⟩ ≈ sin⟨φ⟩`); the linear inertia-generation is exact.

## Falsifiers

| Test | Falsifier |
|---|---|
| Second probabilistic locus | A physical process whose statistics provably cannot reduce to tick selection + deterministic dissipative flow falsifies S3's uniqueness. |
| Anchor in the mechanics | Any structure-producing step shown to require H₀, v_EW, or another measured scale as *input* (not read-out) falsifies S2. |
| Emergence without dissipation | A derivation of the spacetime shadow from a time-reversal-symmetric substrate (λ ≡ 0 fundamentally, no binary irreversible tick) falsifies S1's mechanism — emergence would be kinematic, not dissipative. |
| Non-Boltzmann sampling | Per `f_exit_natural.md`: a demonstrated non-Boltzmann substrate sampling form breaks the least-action clause of S3. |
| Sharp Planck wall | Evidence that the self-sustenance threshold is a discontinuity rather than a crossover revises Part I (per `q_mod2_planck_emergence_audit.md`). |

